target is often the network everyone else depends on.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/chinese-hacking-campaign-hit-a-9th-u-s-telecom-firm-white-house-says", "label": "PBS NewsHour, Chinese hacking campaign hit a 9th US telecom"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Salt Typhoon breached nine US telecoms by December 2024, taking call records and some officials' communications. Officials called voluntary telecom security inadequate.", "sectionKey": "frontier"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$235efd0a-e394-5939-90ab-53f4e8b6fe87$ml$::uuid, $ml$cybersecurity$ml$, $ml$Vulnerability, exploit, zero-day$ml$, 'MICRO_LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-7$ml$, $ml$month-1$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:career$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "cybersecurity-d7-career", "title": "Vulnerability, exploit, zero-day", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "A flaw is not an attack until someone uses it.", "eyebrow": "Day 7 · Vulnerabilities", "headline": "In 2024, 40,009 new vulnerabilities got a public CVE number, about 108 a day.", "fullText": "That was almost 39% more than in 2023. A vulnerability is a flaw in software or hardware; an exploit is the code or method that uses it. A zero-day is a flaw attackers use before the vendor has a fix out. Mandiant tracked 138 flaws disclosed in 2023 being exploited in the wild.", "sources": [{"url": "https://jerrygamblin.com/2025/01/05/2024-cve-data-review/", "label": "Jerry Gamblin, 2024 CVE data review"}, {"url": "https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/time-to-exploit-trends-2023?hl=en", "label": "Google Cloud (Mandiant), time-to-exploit trends 2023"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "cve", "eyebrow": "The ID", "text": "Each public flaw gets a CVE number, so everyone can name the same bug.", "highlight": "Scores run from 0 to 10; 231 flaws scored a perfect 10 in 2024.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "CVE", "definition": "Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures: a public ID for one known flaw."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://jerrygamblin.com/2025/01/05/2024-cve-data-review/", "label": "Jerry Gamblin, 2024 CVE data review"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "zero-day", "eyebrow": "The worst case", "text": "A zero-day is exploited before a fix exists.", "highlight": "An n-day is exploited after the fix is out but not yet installed.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "Zero-day", "definition": "A flaw attackers exploit before the vendor has released a fix."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/time-to-exploit-trends-2023?hl=en", "label": "Google Cloud (Mandiant), time-to-exploit trends 2023"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "choose", "eyebrow": "Why it matters", "title": "Defenders cannot patch everything at once", "body": "At about 108 new flaws a day, teams rank them by how likely and how damaging an attack would be.", "bullets": ["The average severity score in 2024 was 6.67 out of 10."], "sources": [{"url": "https://jerrygamblin.com/2025/01/05/2024-cve-data-review/", "label": "Jerry Gamblin, 2024 CVE data review"}]}, {"kind": "sortSignal", "id": "sort", "prompt": "Flaw, attack tool or fix?", "buckets": ["Vulnerability", "Exploit", "Patch"], "items": [{"text": "A coding mistake in a login page", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "A script that abuses that mistake", "bucket": 1}, {"text": "An update that removes the mistake", "bucket": 2}, {"text": "A misconfigured cloud storage bucket", "bucket": 0}], "explanation": "The flaw is the vulnerability, the tool that uses it is the exploit, the fix is the patch."}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "What makes a vulnerability a zero-day?", "options": ["It is exploited before a fix exists", "It scores a perfect 10 for severity", "It was found on the first day of a release"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "Zero-day means the vendor had zero days of warning: attackers got there first."}, {"id": "lens-career", "kind": "info", "title": "Use the vocabulary precisely", "body": "Vulnerability, exploit, patch, zero-day: using them exactly right is the first test in any security interview.", "eyebrow": "For your interview", "sources": [{"url": "https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/time-to-exploit-trends-2023?hl=en", "label": "Google Cloud (Mandiant), time-to-exploit trends 2023"}, {"url": "https://jerrygamblin.com/2025/01/05/2024-cve-data-review/", "label": "Jerry Gamblin, 2024 CVE data review"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In cyber, the flaw matters less than whether someone can and will exploit it.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/time-to-exploit-trends-2023?hl=en", "label": "Google Cloud (Mandiant), time-to-exploit trends 2023"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "A vulnerability is a flaw, an exploit uses it, and a zero-day is exploited before a fix exists. 40,009 CVEs were published in 2024, about 108 a day.", "sectionKey": "players"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$2eefc10f-c00e-5dcc-9b3d-a31adf6e0677$ml$::uuid, $ml$cybersecurity$ml$, $ml$Vulnerability, exploit, zero-day$ml$, 'MICRO_LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-7$ml$, $ml$month-1$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:invest$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "cybersecurity-d7-invest", "title": "Vulnerability, exploit, zero-day", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "A flaw is not an attack until someone uses it.", "eyebrow": "Day 7 · Vulnerabilities", "headline": "In 2024, 40,009 new vulnerabilities got a public CVE number, about 108 a day.", "fullText": "That was almost 39% more than in 2023. A vulnerability is a flaw in software or hardware; an exploit is the code or method that uses it. A zero-day is a flaw attackers use before the vendor has a fix out. Mandiant tracked 138 flaws disclosed in 2023 being exploited in the wild.", "sources": [{"url": "https://jerrygamblin.com/2025/01/05/2024-cve-data-review/", "label": "Jerry Gamblin, 2024 CVE data review"}, {"url": "https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/time-to-exploit-trends-2023?hl=en", "label": "Google Cloud (Mandiant), time-to-exploit trends 2023"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "cve", "eyebrow": "The ID", "text": "Each public flaw gets a CVE number, so everyone can name the same bug.", "highlight": "Scores run from 0 to 10; 231 flaws scored a perfect 10 in 2024.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "CVE", "definition": "Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures: a public ID for one known flaw."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://jerrygamblin.com/2025/01/05/2024-cve-data-review/", "label": "Jerry Gamblin, 2024 CVE data review"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "zero-day", "eyebrow": "The worst case", "text": "A zero-day is exploited before a fix exists.", "highlight": "An n-day is exploited after the fix is out but not yet installed.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "Zero-day", "definition": "A flaw attackers exploit before the vendor has released a fix."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/time-to-exploit-trends-2023?hl=en", "label": "Google Cloud (Mandiant), time-to-exploit trends 2023"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "choose", "eyebrow": "Why it matters", "title": "Defenders cannot patch everything at once", "body": "At about 108 new flaws a day, teams rank them by how likely and how damaging an attack would be.", "bullets": ["The average severity score in 2024 was 6.67 out of 10."], "sources": [{"url": "https://jerrygamblin.com/2025/01/05/2024-cve-data-review/", "label": "Jerry Gamblin, 2024 CVE data review"}]}, {"kind": "sortSignal", "id": "sort", "prompt": "Flaw, attack tool or fix?", "buckets": ["Vulnerability", "Exploit", "Patch"], "items": [{"text": "A coding mistake in a login page", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "A script that abuses that mistake", "bucket": 1}, {"text": "An update that removes the mistake", "bucket": 2}, {"text": "A misconfigured cloud storage bucket", "bucket": 0}], "explanation": "The flaw is the vulnerability, the tool that uses it is the exploit, the fix is the patch."}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "What makes a vulnerability a zero-day?", "options": ["It is exploited before a fix exists", "It scores a perfect 10 for severity", "It was found on the first day of a release"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "Zero-day means the vendor had zero days of warning: attackers got there first."}, {"id": "lens-invest", "kind": "info", "title": "Volume drives demand", "body": "New public flaws rose almost 39% in a year. More flaws to sort means more demand for tools that rank them.", "eyebrow": "For investors", "sources": [{"url": "https://jerrygamblin.com/2025/01/05/2024-cve-data-review/", "label": "Jerry Gamblin, 2024 CVE data review"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In cyber, the flaw matters less than whether someone can and will exploit it.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/time-to-exploit-trends-2023?hl=en", "label": "Google Cloud (Mandiant), time-to-exploit trends 2023"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "A vulnerability is a flaw, an exploit uses it, and a zero-day is exploited before a fix exists. 40,009 CVEs were published in 2024, about 108 a day.", "sectionKey": "watchlist"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
