arly-usd12-million-in-2024", "label": "TechRadar, Google bug bounty payments in 2024"}, {"url": "https://cyberscoop.com/ibm-cost-data-breach-2025/", "label": "CyberScoop on IBM Cost of a Data Breach 2025"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "scale", "eyebrow": "The track record", "title": "Bounties are now routine", "body": "Google has run reward programs since 2010 and paid $65 million in total.", "bullets": ["Its biggest single 2024 reward was $110,000."], "sources": [{"url": "https://www.techradar.com/pro/security/google-bug-bounty-payments-hit-nearly-usd12-million-in-2024", "label": "TechRadar, Google bug bounty payments in 2024"}]}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-avg", "prompt": "Google paid $11.8 million to 660 researchers in 2024. About how much is that per researcher, in thousands of dollars?", "min": 0, "max": 60, "value": 18, "unit": "K", "explanation": "$11.8 million ÷ 660 is about $18,000 each, though a few big finds take much more."}, {"kind": "faceOff", "id": "face", "prompt": "Which is usually better for the company when a researcher finds a serious flaw?", "left": {"name": "The flaw is reported and paid for", "note": "Fixed before attackers use it"}, "right": {"name": "The flaw stays hidden", "note": "Until someone exploits it"}, "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "Paying for a private report costs far less than a breach."}, {"id": "lens-build_startup", "kind": "info", "title": "Run a bounty early", "body": "A small, well-run bounty program lets outsiders find your flaws before attackers do.", "eyebrow": "For founders", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.techradar.com/pro/security/google-bug-bounty-payments-hit-nearly-usd12-million-in-2024", "label": "TechRadar, Google bug bounty payments in 2024"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In cyber, paying someone to find a flaw is cheaper than paying for the breach.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.techradar.com/pro/security/google-bug-bounty-payments-hit-nearly-usd12-million-in-2024", "label": "TechRadar, Google bug bounty payments in 2024"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Bug bounties pay outsiders to report flaws privately. Google paid $11.8 million to 660 researchers in 2024 and $65 million since 2010.", "sectionKey": "gap"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
