n, NIST releases Cybersecurity Framework 2.0"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "iso", "eyebrow": "ISO/IEC 27001", "text": "ISO 27001 is the best-known standard for running information security as a managed system.", "highlight": "Its current edition was published in October 2022.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "ISMS", "definition": "Information security management system: the policies and processes a company uses to manage security."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://webcf.waybackmachine.org/web/20230531192221/https://www.iso.org/isoiec-27001-information-security.html", "label": "ISO, ISO/IEC 27001 information security management"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "soc2", "eyebrow": "SOC 2", "title": "SOC 2 is an audit report", "body": "A CPA tests a company against up to five criteria. Security is always included; the other four are optional.", "bullets": ["Type I checks the design; Type II tests how controls work over time."], "sources": [{"url": "https://cpl.thalesgroup.com/insights/cybersecurity/what-is-soc-2-compliance", "label": "Thales, what is SOC 2 compliance"}]}, {"kind": "sortSignal", "id": "sort", "prompt": "Which framework is it?", "buckets": ["NIST CSF", "ISO 27001", "SOC 2"], "items": [{"text": "Voluntary, from a US agency", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "Added a Govern function in 2024", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "Lets a company be certified", "bucket": 1}, {"text": "Audited by a CPA", "bucket": 2}, {"text": "Comes in Type I and Type II", "bucket": 2}], "explanation": "NIST CSF is voluntary guidance, ISO 27001 can be certified, and SOC 2 is a CPA audit with two types."}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "A customer wants proof your controls worked over the past year. What should you show?", "options": ["A SOC 2 Type II report", "A SOC 2 Type I report", "A summary of NIST CSF"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "Type II tests how controls operate over a period. Type I only checks their design."}, {"id": "lens-invest", "kind": "info", "title": "Frameworks create recurring spend", "body": "Audits and certifications repeat. That makes compliance work a steady line in security budgets.", "eyebrow": "For investors", "sources": [{"url": "https://cpl.thalesgroup.com/insights/cybersecurity/what-is-soc-2-compliance", "label": "Thales, what is SOC 2 compliance"}, {"url": "https://webcf.waybackmachine.org/web/20230531192221/https://www.iso.org/isoiec-27001-information-security.html", "label": "ISO, ISO/IEC 27001 information security management"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In security, a framework is how you prove to others that you are in control.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.huntonprivacyblog.com/2024/03/04/nist-releases-cybersecurity-framework-2-0/", "label": "Hunton, NIST releases Cybersecurity Framework 2.0"}, {"url": "https://cpl.thalesgroup.com/insights/cybersecurity/what-is-soc-2-compliance", "label": "Thales, what is SOC 2 compliance"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "NIST CSF 2.0 is voluntary guidance with six functions, ISO 27001 can be certified, and SOC 2 is a CPA audit, with Type II testing controls over time.", "sectionKey": "watchlist"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
