tle": "Your buyers will ask", "body": "Business customers ask how vendors handle their data. Know which proof your buyers expect before your first big deal.", "eyebrow": "For founders", "sources": [{"url": "https://cpl.thalesgroup.com/insights/cybersecurity/what-is-soc-2-compliance", "label": "Thales, what is SOC 2 compliance"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In security, a framework is how you prove to others that you are in control.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.huntonprivacyblog.com/2024/03/04/nist-releases-cybersecurity-framework-2-0/", "label": "Hunton, NIST releases Cybersecurity Framework 2.0"}, {"url": "https://cpl.thalesgroup.com/insights/cybersecurity/what-is-soc-2-compliance", "label": "Thales, what is SOC 2 compliance"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "NIST CSF 2.0 is voluntary guidance with six functions, ISO 27001 can be certified, and SOC 2 is a CPA audit, with Type II testing controls over time.", "sectionKey": "money"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$e8bacb53-9bef-5ba1-97a0-6dd05aadb93c$ml$::uuid, $ml$cybersecurity$ml$, $ml$Three ways to prove you are secure$ml$, 'MICRO_LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-13$ml$, $ml$month-1$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:curiosity$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "cybersecurity-d13-curiosity", "title": "Three ways to prove you are secure", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "Same goal, three very different proofs.", "eyebrow": "Day 13 · Frameworks", "headline": "NIST CSF is a voluntary guide, ISO 27001 is a certificate, and SOC 2 is an auditor's report.", "fullText": "NIST released version 2.0 of its Cybersecurity Framework in February 2024 for all organizations, adding a Govern function to its five others. ISO/IEC 27001 sets requirements for an information security management system, and companies can choose to be certified against it. A SOC 2 is an audit by a CPA under criteria from the AICPA.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.huntonprivacyblog.com/2024/03/04/nist-releases-cybersecurity-framework-2-0/", "label": "Hunton, NIST releases Cybersecurity Framework 2.0"}, {"url": "https://webcf.waybackmachine.org/web/20230531192221/https://www.iso.org/isoiec-27001-information-security.html", "label": "ISO, ISO/IEC 27001 information security management"}, {"url": "https://cpl.thalesgroup.com/insights/cybersecurity/what-is-soc-2-compliance", "label": "Thales, what is SOC 2 compliance"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "csf", "eyebrow": "NIST CSF 2.0", "text": "Six functions: Govern, Identify, Protect, Detect, Respond and Recover.", "highlight": "Govern, new in 2024, covers how leaders make security decisions.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "NIST CSF", "definition": "A voluntary US framework for organizing and improving cybersecurity."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://www.huntonprivacyblog.com/2024/03/04/nist-releases-cybersecurity-framework-2-0/", "label": "Hunton, NIST releases Cybersecurity Framework 2.0"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "iso", "eyebrow": "ISO/IEC 27001", "text": "ISO 27001 is the best-known standard for running information security as a managed system.", "highlight": "Its current edition was published in October 2022.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "ISMS", "definition": "Information security management system: the policies and processes a company uses to manage security."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://webcf.waybackmachine.org/web/20230531192221/https://www.iso.org/isoiec-27001-information-security.html", "label": "ISO, ISO/IEC 27001 information security management"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "soc2", "eyebrow": "SOC 2", "title": "SOC 2 is an audit report", "body": "A CPA tests a company against up to five criteria. Security is always included; the other four are optional.", "bullets": ["Type I checks the design; Type II tests how controls work over time."], "sources": [{"url": "https://cpl.thalesgroup.com/insights/cybersecurity/what-is-soc-2-compliance", "label": "Thales, what is SOC 2 compliance"}]}, {"kind": "sortSignal", "id": "sort", "prompt": "Which framework is it?", "buckets": ["NIST CSF", "ISO 27001", "SOC 2"], "items": [{"text": "Voluntary, from a US agency", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "Added a Govern function in 2024", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "Lets a company be certified", "bucket": 1}, {"text": "Audited by a CPA", "bucket": 2}, {"text": "Comes in Type I and Type II", "bucket": 2}], "explanation": "NIST CSF is voluntary guidance, ISO 27001 can be certified, and SOC 2 is a CPA audit with two types."}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "A customer wants proof your controls worked over the past year. What should you show?", "options": ["A SOC 2 Type II report", "A SOC 2 Type I report", "A summary of NIST CSF"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "Type II tests how controls operate over a period. Type I only checks their design."}, {"id": "lens-curiosity", "kind": "info", "title": "Three kinds of proof", "body": "A guide, a certificate and an audit report: security has three main ways to show it is under control.", "eyebrow": "Why it matters", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.huntonprivacyblog.com/2024/03/04/nist-releases-cybersecurity-framework-2-0/", "label": "Hunton, NIST releases Cybersecurity Framework 2.0"}, {"url": "https://webcf.waybackmachine.org/web/20230531192221/https://www.iso.org/isoiec-27001-information-security.html", "label": "ISO, ISO/IEC 27001 information security management"}, {"url": "https://cpl.thalesgroup.com/insights/cybersecurity/what-is-soc-2-compliance", "label": "Thales, what is SOC 2 compliance"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In security, a framework is how you prove to others that you are in control.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.huntonprivacyblog.com/2024/03/04/nist-releases-cybersecurity-framework-2-0/", "label": "Hunton, NIST releases Cybersecurity Framework 2.0"}, {"url": "https://cpl.thalesgroup.com/insights/cybersecurity/what-is-soc-2-compliance", "label": "Thales, what is SOC 2 compliance"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "NIST CSF 2.0 is voluntary guidance with six functions, ISO 27001 can be certified, and SOC 2 is a CPA audit, with Type II testing controls over time.", "sectionKey": "basics"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$c5f15ceb-e441-5d14-b41f-bf1b8ee82979$ml$::uuid, $ml$cybersecurity$ml$, $ml$Why startups pay for SOC 2$ml$, 'MICRO_LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-14$ml$, $ml$month-1$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:career$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "cybersecurity-d14-career", "title": "Why startups pay for SOC 2", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "Compliance became a sales tool.", "eyebrow": "Day 14 · The money", "headline": "In July 2024, Vanta, which automates SOC 2 and ISO 27001 work, raised $150 million at a $2.45 billion valuation.", "fullText": "Vanta had more than 8,000 customers. Business buyers ask whether a vendor can be trusted with their data, and audits are how vendors answer. Its CEO put it simply: earning credit for security work really means revenue.", "sources": [{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2024/07/24/trust-management-platform-vanta-raises-150m-series-c-now-valued-at-2-45b", "label": "TechCrunch, Vanta raises $150M at $2.45B"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "buyer", "eyebrow": "Who pays", "text": "Vendors pay for audits because their customers ask for proof.", "highlight": "Without it, security reviews can stall a deal.", "sources": [{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2024/07/24/trust-management-platform-vanta-raises-150m-series-c-now-valued-at-2-45b", "label": "TechCrunch, Vanta raises $150M at $2.45B"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "growth", "eyebrow": "The market", "text": "Vanta's value rose from $1.6 billion in 2022 to $2.45 billion in 2024.", "highlight": "Investors bet that compliance is a durable, recurring need.", "sources": [{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2024/07/24/trust-management-platform-vanta-raises-150m-series-c-now-valued-at-2-45b", "label": "TechCrunch, Vanta raises $150M at $2.45B"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "automate", "eyebrow": "The product", "title": "Automating the evidence", "body": "Platforms like Vanta collect proof from a company's systems so audits take less manual work.", "bullets": ["It began with ISO 27001, HIPAA and SOC 2."], "sources": [{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2024/07/24/trust-management-platform-vanta-raises-150m-series-c-now-valued-at-2-45b", "label": "TechCrunch, Vanta raises $150M at $2.45B"}]}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-val", "prompt": "Vanta was valued at $1.6 billion in 2022 and $2.45 billion in 2024. By about what percent did its value rise?", "min": 0, "max": 150, "value": 53, "unit": "%", "explanation": "$2.45 billion is about 53% more than $1.6 billion."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "Your startup is close to a deal with a large bank. Their security team asks for a SOC 2 report you do not have.", "prompt": "What do you do?", "options": ["Tell them your product is secure enough", "Start a SOC 2 and share the timeline", "Walk away from the deal and move on"], "consequences": ["Without proof, their security review can stall.", "A credible plan can keep the deal moving.", "You lose a customer you could have won."], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "Buyers want evidence. A real audit underway is far stronger than assurances."}, {"id": "lens-career", "kind": "info", "title": "Compliance roles open doors", "body": "Every SOC 2 needs people who gather evidence and fix gaps. It is a common entry point into security.", "eyebrow": "For your interview", "sources": [{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2024/07/24/trust-management-platform-vanta-raises-150m-series-c-now-valued-at-2-45b", "label": "TechCrunch, Vanta raises $150M at $2.45B"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In B2B security, proof of trust is part of what you sell.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2024/07/24/trust-management-platform-vanta-raises-150m-series-c-now-valued-at-2-45b", "label": "TechCrunch, Vanta raises $150M at $2.45B"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Vendors pay for SOC 2 and ISO 27001 because buyers ask for proof. Vanta, which automates that work, was valued at $2.45 billion in 2024.", "sectionKey": "how_money_moves"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
