IS2 rules"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "scope", "eyebrow": "Who it covers", "title": "Far more than before", "body": "NIS2 widened the scope well beyond the first NIS rules, including cloud and data center providers.", "sources": [{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}]}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "An essential entity has €2 billion in worldwide turnover. What is its maximum NIS2 fine?", "options": ["€10 million", "€40 million", "€2 million"], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "2% of €2 billion is €40 million, which is greater than €10 million."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "Your EU cloud company finds a significant intrusion at 9 a.m. The facts are still unclear.", "prompt": "What do you do about reporting?", "options": ["Warn regulators within 24 hours", "Wait until you know everything", "Report only if data was stolen"], "consequences": ["The rule expects a warning before you have all the facts.", "Waiting can miss the 24-hour deadline.", "NIS2 covers significant incidents, not only data theft."], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "The early warning is designed to come fast, with details to follow."}, {"id": "lens-build_startup", "kind": "info", "title": "Fast reporting needs tools", "body": "A 24-hour warning leaves little time to gather facts. Tools that speed incident reporting have buyers.", "eyebrow": "For founders", "sources": [{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In cyber regulation, the reporting clock starts before you know the full story.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "NIS2 requires an early warning within 24 hours of a significant incident. Essential entities face fines of up to €10 million or 2% of worldwide turnover.", "sectionKey": "incumbents"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
