22 White House memo set zero trust goals for federal agencies to meet by the end of fiscal 2024.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/M-22-09.pdf", "label": "OMB memo M-22-09, federal zero trust strategy"}]}, {"kind": "sortSignal", "id": "sort", "prompt": "Perimeter model or zero trust?", "buckets": ["Perimeter", "Zero trust"], "items": [{"text": "Inside the office network means trusted", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "One VPN login opens everything", "bucket": 0}, {"text": "Every session is verified", "bucket": 1}, {"text": "Device health is checked each time", "bucket": 1}], "explanation": "The perimeter model trusts location. Zero trust verifies each access."}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "Under zero trust, what earns a device access?", "options": ["Being plugged into the office network", "Passing checks before each session", "Having connected safely last week"], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "Authentication and authorization happen before every session, not once."}, {"id": "lens-curiosity", "kind": "info", "title": "No more castle walls", "body": "Zero trust treats every access like a stranger at the door, even from inside the office.", "eyebrow": "Why it matters", "sources": [{"url": "https://csrc.nist.gov/Pubs/sp/800/207/Final", "label": "NIST SP 800-207, Zero Trust Architecture"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In network security, location is not identity.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://csrc.nist.gov/Pubs/sp/800/207/Final", "label": "NIST SP 800-207, Zero Trust Architecture"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "NIST defined zero trust in 2020 as granting no trust based on network location. Every user and device is verified before each session.", "sectionKey": "basics"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$0ea792a9-0858-5491-9b04-46f52b455dfa$ml$::uuid, $ml$cybersecurity$ml$, $ml$Selling zero trust by subscription$ml$, 'MICRO_LESSON', ARRAY[$ml$MICRO_LESSON$ml$, $ml$day-26$ml$, $ml$month-1$ml$, $ml$handwritten-v1$ml$, $ml$goal:career$ml$, $ml$level:beginner$ml$, $ml$level:intermediate$ml$, $ml$level:advanced$ml$]::text[], 5, now(), '{}'::jsonb, $ml${"id": "cybersecurity-d26-career", "title": "Selling zero trust by subscription", "exercises": [{"id": "open", "kind": "coldOpen", "kicker": "Security moved into the cloud, and so did the bills.", "eyebrow": "Day 26 · The money", "headline": "Zscaler, a cloud zero trust vendor, earned $2.67 billion in fiscal 2025, up 23%.", "fullText": "Instead of boxes in a company's server room, Zscaler routes users' traffic through its cloud, checking each connection. Customers pay by subscription. Its CEO said annual recurring revenue topped $3 billion, and it guided to about $3.7 billion in revenue for fiscal 2026.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.constellationr.com/insights/news/zscaler-delivers-strong-q4-fiscal-2026-outlook", "label": "Constellation Research, Zscaler fiscal 2025 results"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "subscription", "eyebrow": "The model", "text": "Customers rent security as a service instead of buying hardware.", "highlight": "That turns one-off sales into recurring revenue.", "keyTerms": [{"term": "ARR", "definition": "Annual recurring revenue: the yearly value of active subscriptions."}], "sources": [{"url": "https://www.constellationr.com/insights/news/zscaler-delivers-strong-q4-fiscal-2026-outlook", "label": "Constellation Research, Zscaler fiscal 2025 results"}]}, {"kind": "microInsight", "id": "growth", "eyebrow": "The growth", "text": "Revenue grew 23% in fiscal 2025.", "highlight": "The 2026 guidance was $3.68 to $3.7 billion.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.constellationr.com/insights/news/zscaler-delivers-strong-q4-fiscal-2026-outlook", "label": "Constellation Research, Zscaler fiscal 2025 results"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "why", "eyebrow": "Why it sells", "title": "Remote work broke the perimeter", "body": "When staff work from anywhere, checking each connection in the cloud fits better than a wall around one office.", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.constellationr.com/insights/news/zscaler-delivers-strong-q4-fiscal-2026-outlook", "label": "Constellation Research, Zscaler fiscal 2025 results"}, {"url": "https://csrc.nist.gov/Pubs/sp/800/207/Final", "label": "NIST SP 800-207, Zero Trust Architecture"}]}, {"kind": "numberSense", "id": "ns-growth", "prompt": "By what percent did Zscaler's revenue grow in fiscal 2025?", "min": 0, "max": 60, "value": 23, "unit": "%", "explanation": "23%, to $2.67 billion."}, {"kind": "faceOff", "id": "face", "prompt": "Which revenue is easier for investors to predict?", "left": {"name": "One-time hardware sales", "note": "Each year starts from zero"}, "right": {"name": "Yearly subscriptions", "note": "Most customers renew"}, "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "Recurring subscriptions carry over from year to year, so they are easier to forecast."}, {"id": "lens-career", "kind": "info", "title": "Know the delivery model", "body": "Security now sells as cloud subscriptions. Knowing why helps in sales, product and engineering roles alike.", "eyebrow": "For your interview", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.constellationr.com/insights/news/zscaler-delivers-strong-q4-fiscal-2026-outlook", "label": "Constellation Research, Zscaler fiscal 2025 results"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In security, recurring revenue rewards vendors who stay useful every month.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://www.constellationr.com/insights/news/zscaler-delivers-strong-q4-fiscal-2026-outlook", "label": "Constellation Research, Zscaler fiscal 2025 results"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "Zscaler sells zero trust from the cloud by subscription: $2.67 billion in fiscal 2025 revenue, up 23%, with ARR above $3 billion.", "sectionKey": "how_money_moves"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
