chCrunch, CISA orders agencies to disconnect Ivanti VPNs"}]}, {"kind": "info", "id": "hunt", "eyebrow": "After the unplug", "title": "Assume they got further", "body": "Agencies also had to hunt for threats on connected systems and audit privileged accounts.", "sources": [{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2024/02/01/cisa-federal-agencies-disconnect-ivanti-vpn", "label": "TechCrunch, CISA orders agencies to disconnect Ivanti VPNs"}]}, {"kind": "multipleChoice", "id": "mc", "prompt": "Why did CISA order the Ivanti VPNs unplugged instead of patched?", "options": ["Attackers were bypassing the fixes", "Ivanti had stopped supporting the VPN", "The VPNs were slowing agency networks"], "correctIndex": 0, "explanation": "Published mitigations were being bypassed, so disconnecting was the safer step."}, {"kind": "theCall", "id": "call", "situation": "Your company runs the same VPN. A patch is out, but attackers are reportedly getting around it.", "prompt": "What do you do?", "options": ["Patch it and move on", "Take it offline and rebuild clean", "Leave it, since you are not a target"], "consequences": ["Fixes were being bypassed.", "CISA required a fresh, patched install for agencies.", "At least 2,200 devices were already compromised."], "correctIndex": 1, "explanation": "When attackers beat the fix, rebuild clean and hunt for intruders."}, {"id": "lens-build_startup", "kind": "info", "title": "Shrink the edge", "body": "Every internet-facing box is a target. Designs that hide services from the internet answer that.", "eyebrow": "For founders", "sources": [{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2024/02/01/cisa-federal-agencies-disconnect-ivanti-vpn", "label": "TechCrunch, CISA orders agencies to disconnect Ivanti VPNs"}, {"url": "https://csrc.nist.gov/Pubs/sp/800/207/Final", "label": "NIST SP 800-207, Zero Trust Architecture"}]}, {"id": "rule", "kind": "microInsight", "text": "In network security, the device facing the internet is the one attackers hit first.", "eyebrow": "The rule", "sources": [{"url": "https://techcrunch.com/2024/02/01/cisa-federal-agencies-disconnect-ivanti-vpn", "label": "TechCrunch, CISA orders agencies to disconnect Ivanti VPNs"}]}, {"id": "say-it", "kind": "sayIt", "takeaway": "In February 2024, CISA gave agencies 48 hours to disconnect Ivanti VPNs as attackers bypassed fixes. Edge devices are prime targets.", "sectionKey": "who_hurts"}]}$ml$::jsonb),
