($ml$5783b5af-f612-5363-a88a-61c61f49d1c9$ml$::uuid, $ml$3199fc4b-1535-5c8a-a58e-814efc47fe8c$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The target$ml$, $ml$The goal was to know who calls whom, then listen to chosen targets. The FBI said most targets were involved in government or politics.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/chinese-hacking-campaign-hit-a-9th-u-s-telecom-firm-white-house-says", "label": "PBS NewsHour, Chinese hacking campaign hit a 9th US telecom"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$169cf6fe-9829-57e9-8534-62dcd61df3d5$ml$::uuid, $ml$3199fc4b-1535-5c8a-a58e-814efc47fe8c$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The scale$ml$, $ml$At least eight US telecoms were named first, then a ninth. Officials said dozens of countries were affected.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/chinese-hacking-campaign-hit-a-9th-u-s-telecom-firm-white-house-says", "label": "PBS NewsHour, Chinese hacking campaign hit a 9th US telecom"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$5967d2a4-c749-5a54-94c8-cba814332bdc$ml$::uuid, $ml$3199fc4b-1535-5c8a-a58e-814efc47fe8c$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Voluntary security was not enough$ml$, $ml$Telecom security had largely been voluntary. Officials called that inadequate and pushed for required practices.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/chinese-hacking-campaign-hit-a-9th-u-s-telecom-firm-white-house-says", "label": "PBS NewsHour, Chinese hacking campaign hit a 9th US telecom"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$430b9fc8-25de-5dd9-a4e6-05d530168b15$ml$::uuid, $ml$3199fc4b-1535-5c8a-a58e-814efc47fe8c$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Spies in the phone system$ml$, $ml$Hackers inside nine US phone companies could see call records and reach some officials' communications.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/chinese-hacking-campaign-hit-a-9th-u-s-telecom-firm-white-house-says", "label": "PBS NewsHour, Chinese hacking campaign hit a 9th US telecom"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$2dafce4e-8ab8-550f-9354-f0db0b5fab33$ml$::uuid, $ml$3199fc4b-1535-5c8a-a58e-814efc47fe8c$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cyber, the most valuable target is often the network everyone else depends on.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/chinese-hacking-campaign-hit-a-9th-u-s-telecom-firm-white-house-says", "label": "PBS NewsHour, Chinese hacking campaign hit a 9th US telecom"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$66314c55-f4e9-5f39-a97c-8a7d97b52fcb$ml$::uuid, $ml$235efd0a-e394-5939-90ab-53f4e8b6fe87$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 7 · Vulnerabilities$ml$, $ml$In 2024, 40,009 new vulnerabilities got a public CVE number, about 108 a day. That was almost 39% more than in 2023. A vulnerability is a flaw in software or hardware; an exploit is the code or method that uses it. A zero-day is a flaw attackers use before the vendor has a fix out. Mandiant tracked 138 flaws disclosed in 2023 being exploited in the wild.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://jerrygamblin.com/2025/01/05/2024-cve-data-review/", "label": "Jerry Gamblin, 2024 CVE data review"}, {"url": "https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/time-to-exploit-trends-2023?hl=en", "label": "Google Cloud (Mandiant), time-to-exploit trends 2023"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$b464f703-0f58-5ef0-ad15-f006ee350600$ml$::uuid, $ml$235efd0a-e394-5939-90ab-53f4e8b6fe87$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The ID$ml$, $ml$Each public flaw gets a CVE number, so everyone can name the same bug. Scores run from 0 to 10; 231 flaws scored a perfect 10 in 2024.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://jerrygamblin.com/2025/01/05/2024-cve-data-review/", "label": "Jerry Gamblin, 2024 CVE data review"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$16a9947f-a0b3-55ac-af8e-800f0b050d80$ml$::uuid, $ml$235efd0a-e394-5939-90ab-53f4e8b6fe87$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The worst case$ml$, $ml$A zero-day is exploited before a fix exists. An n-day is exploited after the fix is out but not yet installed.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/time-to-exploit-trends-2023?hl=en", "label": "Google Cloud (Mandiant), time-to-exploit trends 2023"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$83f02a04-7fb2-5a97-9858-8c85aed184c9$ml$::uuid, $ml$235efd0a-e394-5939-90ab-53f4e8b6fe87$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Defenders cannot patch everything at once$ml$, $ml$At about 108 new flaws a day, teams rank them by how likely and how damaging an attack would be. The average severity score in 2024 was 6.67 out of 10.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://jerrygamblin.com/2025/01/05/2024-cve-data-review/", "label": "Jerry Gamblin, 2024 CVE data review"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$5e9ac1c7-2451-5f6f-8153-e241de22c544$ml$::uuid, $ml$235efd0a-e394-5939-90ab-53f4e8b6fe87$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Use the vocabulary precisely$ml$, $ml$Vulnerability, exploit, patch, zero-day: using them exactly right is the first test in any security interview.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/time-to-exploit-trends-2023?hl=en", "label": "Google Cloud (Mandiant), time-to-exploit trends 2023"}, {"url": "https://jerrygamblin.com/2025/01/05/2024-cve-data-review/", "label": "Jerry Gamblin, 2024 CVE data review"}]$ml$::jsonb),
