($ml$b10f9ad9-ea13-511e-ae62-294a8f76223a$ml$::uuid, $ml$ae20bd6c-14cc-5221-9f62-5cd9033680b3$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The math$ml$, $ml$For a company Google's size, $11.8 million a year is cheap insurance. The average US breach cost $10.22 million in 2025.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.techradar.com/pro/security/google-bug-bounty-payments-hit-nearly-usd12-million-in-2024", "label": "TechRadar, Google bug bounty payments in 2024"}, {"url": "https://cyberscoop.com/ibm-cost-data-breach-2025/", "label": "CyberScoop on IBM Cost of a Data Breach 2025"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$dbe23bcf-a42e-5b98-b6db-c8a61439d311$ml$::uuid, $ml$ae20bd6c-14cc-5221-9f62-5cd9033680b3$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Bounties are now routine$ml$, $ml$Google has run reward programs since 2010 and paid $65 million in total. Its biggest single 2024 reward was $110,000.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.techradar.com/pro/security/google-bug-bounty-payments-hit-nearly-usd12-million-in-2024", "label": "TechRadar, Google bug bounty payments in 2024"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$9025f340-5cfb-59b9-8aeb-34d2fc511488$ml$::uuid, $ml$ae20bd6c-14cc-5221-9f62-5cd9033680b3$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Paid to hack$ml$, $ml$660 people earned money from Google in 2024 for finding flaws, one of them $110,000 for a single report.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.techradar.com/pro/security/google-bug-bounty-payments-hit-nearly-usd12-million-in-2024", "label": "TechRadar, Google bug bounty payments in 2024"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$0f9e865d-3d80-57d2-8044-5476a58c3d86$ml$::uuid, $ml$ae20bd6c-14cc-5221-9f62-5cd9033680b3$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cyber, paying someone to find a flaw is cheaper than paying for the breach.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.techradar.com/pro/security/google-bug-bounty-payments-hit-nearly-usd12-million-in-2024", "label": "TechRadar, Google bug bounty payments in 2024"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$11ae5fed-eead-5800-bc82-4357c81f9478$ml$::uuid, $ml$d912c173-3101-5b7a-ad7b-13472915f18d$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 9 · The power$ml$, $ml$Under CISA's directive BOD 22-01, US civilian agencies must fix listed flaws within two weeks. CISA keeps the Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog. A flaw goes on it only with a CVE ID, clear remediation guidance and reliable evidence it is being exploited in the wild. Agencies get two weeks for most listed flaws and six months for those with CVE IDs from before 2021.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cisa.gov/binding-operational-directive-22-01", "label": "CISA, Binding Operational Directive 22-01"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$37dce5fa-6f5b-5bba-b6f4-8f421c222fd9$ml$::uuid, $ml$d912c173-3101-5b7a-ad7b-13472915f18d$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The bar$ml$, $ml$The catalog lists only flaws attackers are actually using. That turns 40,000 a year into a short, urgent list.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cisa.gov/binding-operational-directive-22-01", "label": "CISA, Binding Operational Directive 22-01"}, {"url": "https://jerrygamblin.com/2025/01/05/2024-cve-data-review/", "label": "Jerry Gamblin, 2024 CVE data review"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$1a5676ef-a596-57ef-8e06-be4c27c8e452$ml$::uuid, $ml$d912c173-3101-5b7a-ad7b-13472915f18d$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The follow-up$ml$, $ml$Agencies must report their progress, not just promise it. Status goes to a federal dashboard CISA can watch.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cisa.gov/binding-operational-directive-22-01", "label": "CISA, Binding Operational Directive 22-01"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$31ab8357-b1be-54cb-a598-9482e988461c$ml$::uuid, $ml$d912c173-3101-5b7a-ad7b-13472915f18d$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$CISA sets the deadline$ml$, $ml$Once a flaw is listed, federal agencies have no choice about urgency. CISA can shorten deadlines in cases of grave risk.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cisa.gov/binding-operational-directive-22-01", "label": "CISA, Binding Operational Directive 22-01"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$e560718f-8eb6-5930-97bd-46b09a02ebf7$ml$::uuid, $ml$d912c173-3101-5b7a-ad7b-13472915f18d$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Mention the KEV catalog$ml$, $ml$Saying you would patch KEV-listed flaws first shows you know how real teams prioritize.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cisa.gov/binding-operational-directive-22-01", "label": "CISA, Binding Operational Directive 22-01"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$47cf63d5-71ba-5466-9c4d-82b85a2ffa42$ml$::uuid, $ml$d912c173-3101-5b7a-ad7b-13472915f18d$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cyber, whoever decides what is urgent shapes where defenders spend their time.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cisa.gov/binding-operational-directive-22-01", "label": "CISA, Binding Operational Directive 22-01"}]$ml$::jsonb),
