($ml$eb18b5fc-dc14-52c5-8c81-8f1c60356997$ml$::uuid, $ml$ea1deba3-7d7c-59b0-b116-77263b0f672a$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Averages hide long tails$ml$, $ml$Mandiant left out 15 outliers. With them, the 2023 average rises from five days to 47.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/time-to-exploit-trends-2023?hl=en", "label": "Google Cloud (Mandiant), time-to-exploit trends 2023"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$cc0dca0c-0c1e-5f74-9da9-e574aef04c8c$ml$::uuid, $ml$ea1deba3-7d7c-59b0-b116-77263b0f672a$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$From two months to five days$ml$, $ml$Attackers once took about two months to use a new flaw. By 2023, it was five days on average.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/time-to-exploit-trends-2023?hl=en", "label": "Google Cloud (Mandiant), time-to-exploit trends 2023"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$876629cc-a75c-5251-8cfb-ced480ad9e3a$ml$::uuid, $ml$ea1deba3-7d7c-59b0-b116-77263b0f672a$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cyber, defenders are racing a clock that keeps getting shorter.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/time-to-exploit-trends-2023?hl=en", "label": "Google Cloud (Mandiant), time-to-exploit trends 2023"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$4ddbbba5-7c6c-5a0c-903d-481154799f09$ml$::uuid, $ml$4ef6b9b9-5990-5c41-bd59-5eb34ab62c12$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 11 · The risk$ml$, $ml$In July 2022, a US review board called the Log4j flaw an endemic vulnerability. Log4j is a free logging library used across huge amounts of software. Its flaw, found by Alibaba in late 2021, let attackers take over systems. The Cyber Safety Review Board warned that unpatched versions will remain in systems for the next decade, if not longer, and said open-source developers are thinly resourced.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://therecord.media/first-cyber-safety-review-board-report-finds-log4j-has-become-an-endemic-vulnerability/", "label": "The Record, Log4j is an endemic vulnerability"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$ef5b5049-484d-5aa2-a79b-c438b707ea2c$ml$::uuid, $ml$4ef6b9b9-5990-5c41-bd59-5eb34ab62c12$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The problem$ml$, $ml$Companies often did not know Log4j was inside their products. You cannot patch what you do not know you run.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://therecord.media/first-cyber-safety-review-board-report-finds-log4j-has-become-an-endemic-vulnerability/", "label": "The Record, Log4j is an endemic vulnerability"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$3f08e8b1-c852-5ee5-9643-033472f067ef$ml$::uuid, $ml$4ef6b9b9-5990-5c41-bd59-5eb34ab62c12$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The verdict$ml$, $ml$"This event is not over. The risk remains," the board's chair said. The board made 19 recommendations.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://therecord.media/first-cyber-safety-review-board-report-finds-log4j-has-become-an-endemic-vulnerability/", "label": "The Record, Log4j is an endemic vulnerability"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$d168a976-71bc-5906-beb5-5683718b3612$ml$::uuid, $ml$4ef6b9b9-5990-5c41-bd59-5eb34ab62c12$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Free code, thin support$ml$, $ml$Critical software is often kept up by a few volunteers. The board called for better security practices in open source.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://therecord.media/first-cyber-safety-review-board-report-finds-log4j-has-become-an-endemic-vulnerability/", "label": "The Record, Log4j is an endemic vulnerability"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$42ce95fb-0775-5935-824b-4ceaea9b9eef$ml$::uuid, $ml$4ef6b9b9-5990-5c41-bd59-5eb34ab62c12$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Know your dependencies$ml$, $ml$Log4j showed teams often did not know what was inside their software. Inventory skills are in demand.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://therecord.media/first-cyber-safety-review-board-report-finds-log4j-has-become-an-endemic-vulnerability/", "label": "The Record, Log4j is an endemic vulnerability"}]$ml$::jsonb),
