($ml$3f98815d-febf-5da5-8f6b-435463457440$ml$::uuid, $ml$281f4a90-ff3b-5a48-9ecf-9574090101af$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cyber, the risk you inherit from other people's code is still your risk.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://therecord.media/first-cyber-safety-review-board-report-finds-log4j-has-become-an-endemic-vulnerability/", "label": "The Record, Log4j is an endemic vulnerability"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$72abf286-d3ca-586b-97b8-2b42fd4a7446$ml$::uuid, $ml$7622e79d-023a-56b0-ad15-f6c904899e7f$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 12 · Where it breaks$ml$, $ml$In March 2024, an engineer noticed SSH logins taking 500 milliseconds longer and found a backdoor. Andres Freund traced the delay to malicious code in XZ Utils, a compression tool used in Linux. It was shipped in versions 5.6.0 and 5.6.1 and signed by an account that had contributed to the project for several years. Because those versions were mostly in early test releases of Linux, the backdoor was caught before wide use.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.elastic.co/cn/security-labs/500ms-to-midnight", "label": "Elastic Security Labs, the xz backdoor"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$b7fdf1ac-6420-5171-8c94-5f6fcb4e08be$ml$::uuid, $ml$7622e79d-023a-56b0-ad15-f6c904899e7f$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The method$ml$, $ml$The attacker spent years earning trust as a contributor. Then used that trust to ship the backdoor.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.elastic.co/cn/security-labs/500ms-to-midnight", "label": "Elastic Security Labs, the xz backdoor"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$7990c87e-0d1e-5373-9fdd-ed845a7fe30c$ml$::uuid, $ml$7622e79d-023a-56b0-ad15-f6c904899e7f$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The save$ml$, $ml$It was caught by curiosity, not by a security tool. One engineer wondered why logins were half a second slow.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.elastic.co/cn/security-labs/500ms-to-midnight", "label": "Elastic Security Labs, the xz backdoor"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$b03a7ecb-000c-53f8-9abc-50d2710de2e2$ml$::uuid, $ml$7622e79d-023a-56b0-ad15-f6c904899e7f$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Who checks the maintainers?$ml$, $ml$Key open-source tools often depend on a handful of volunteers. Few safeguards check who earns commit rights. It was tracked as CVE-2024-3094.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.elastic.co/cn/security-labs/500ms-to-midnight", "label": "Elastic Security Labs, the xz backdoor"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$7de6743e-b476-5981-859a-a2e33ab75033$ml$::uuid, $ml$7622e79d-023a-56b0-ad15-f6c904899e7f$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Curiosity is a security skill$ml$, $ml$The xz backdoor was caught because someone asked why logins were slow. Mention it when asked what makes a good analyst.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.elastic.co/cn/security-labs/500ms-to-midnight", "label": "Elastic Security Labs, the xz backdoor"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$a53bc954-0288-507f-853d-60a0339886d2$ml$::uuid, $ml$7622e79d-023a-56b0-ad15-f6c904899e7f$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cyber, trusted people can be the attack path, not just flawed code.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.elastic.co/cn/security-labs/500ms-to-midnight", "label": "Elastic Security Labs, the xz backdoor"}]$ml$::jsonb),
