($ml$42ee2e49-3b87-5503-940c-8d6288721645$ml$::uuid, $ml$a9793996-58d5-5248-8345-12a0f99f833f$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 13 · Frameworks$ml$, $ml$NIST CSF is a voluntary guide, ISO 27001 is a certificate, and SOC 2 is an auditor's report. NIST released version 2.0 of its Cybersecurity Framework in February 2024 for all organizations, adding a Govern function to its five others. ISO/IEC 27001 sets requirements for an information security management system, and companies can choose to be certified against it. A SOC 2 is an audit by a CPA under criteria from the AICPA.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.huntonprivacyblog.com/2024/03/04/nist-releases-cybersecurity-framework-2-0/", "label": "Hunton, NIST releases Cybersecurity Framework 2.0"}, {"url": "https://webcf.waybackmachine.org/web/20230531192221/https://www.iso.org/isoiec-27001-information-security.html", "label": "ISO, ISO/IEC 27001 information security management"}, {"url": "https://cpl.thalesgroup.com/insights/cybersecurity/what-is-soc-2-compliance", "label": "Thales, what is SOC 2 compliance"}]$ml$::jsonb),
