($ml$0e889695-4d56-56f3-b2a1-8c7577434e4a$ml$::uuid, $ml$1eb2452f-ea29-53ca-adc7-0c32e06907b0$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 15 · The power$ml$, $ml$In March 2026, the FedRAMP Marketplace listed 502 authorized cloud services, with 75 more in progress. FedRAMP, run by the General Services Administration, gives agencies one standard way to assess, authorize and monitor the security of cloud products. In March 2025 it launched FedRAMP 20x, a revamp built on automation to speed approvals, with the goal of growing to thousands of services.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.meritalk.com/articles/fedramp-hits-500-authorized-cloud-services/", "label": "MeriTalk, FedRAMP hits 500 authorized cloud services"}]$ml$::jsonb),
