($ml$679bb4f2-20d9-5910-b428-a56125131e6f$ml$::uuid, $ml$63bc187e-d4b6-56a8-b94e-203380586657$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The levels$ml$, $ml$Level 1: 15 requirements. Level 2: 110. Level 3: 24 more on top. The level depends on how sensitive the data is.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.faegredrinker.com/en/insights/publications/2025/9/department-of-defense-publishes-final-rule-to-implement-and-enforce-cybersecurity-standards-for-contractors", "label": "Faegre Drinker, DoD final CMMC rule"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$12bd3d17-3225-5173-a40c-8077a3bb91ad$ml$::uuid, $ml$63bc187e-d4b6-56a8-b94e-203380586657$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$Who it hits$ml$, $ml$Nearly 230,000 small businesses are among those affected. Small firms face the same rules as large ones.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.faegredrinker.com/en/insights/publications/2025/9/department-of-defense-publishes-final-rule-to-implement-and-enforce-cybersecurity-standards-for-contractors", "label": "Faegre Drinker, DoD final CMMC rule"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$89170c7b-c1c4-5061-97ab-5f5351175382$ml$::uuid, $ml$63bc187e-d4b6-56a8-b94e-203380586657$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Phased in over three years$ml$, $ml$From November 2025, program offices add requirements where needed. From November 10, 2028, they apply to all relevant contracts.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.faegredrinker.com/en/insights/publications/2025/9/department-of-defense-publishes-final-rule-to-implement-and-enforce-cybersecurity-standards-for-contractors", "label": "Faegre Drinker, DoD final CMMC rule"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$fdafe98d-eff6-51bd-aa97-a0e73a89a779$ml$::uuid, $ml$63bc187e-d4b6-56a8-b94e-203380586657$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Security as a contract term$ml$, $ml$To keep defense work, hundreds of thousands of companies must now prove they meet set security rules.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.faegredrinker.com/en/insights/publications/2025/9/department-of-defense-publishes-final-rule-to-implement-and-enforce-cybersecurity-standards-for-contractors", "label": "Faegre Drinker, DoD final CMMC rule"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$113e3954-cba5-56c8-94c6-da300a4422bc$ml$::uuid, $ml$63bc187e-d4b6-56a8-b94e-203380586657$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In defense contracting, security is now a condition of getting paid.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.faegredrinker.com/en/insights/publications/2025/9/department-of-defense-publishes-final-rule-to-implement-and-enforce-cybersecurity-standards-for-contractors", "label": "Faegre Drinker, DoD final CMMC rule"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$5e5157d2-dfba-5941-92b4-0effd2a98f98$ml$::uuid, $ml$9fd05b5c-e974-5046-9cff-3c16ff1f40ea$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 17 · The rule$ml$, $ml$Since October 2024, companies under the EU's NIS2 rules must send an early warning within 24 hours of a significant incident. A fuller notification follows within 48 hours of that warning, and a final report within a month. Essential entities face fines of up to €10 million or 2% of worldwide annual turnover, whichever is greater. Important entities face up to €7 million or 1.4%.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$6dd93934-2884-5d57-bc0a-37cf59fd31e4$ml$::uuid, $ml$9fd05b5c-e974-5046-9cff-3c16ff1f40ea$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The clock$ml$, $ml$24 hours for an early warning, 48 more for the notification. Then one month for a final report with the root cause.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$2690cde3-5601-57be-b497-e66020fb059a$ml$::uuid, $ml$9fd05b5c-e974-5046-9cff-3c16ff1f40ea$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The stick$ml$, $ml$Fines scale with company size: up to 2% of worldwide turnover. For a big company, that can far exceed €10 million.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$fa4b58db-1beb-572d-8294-2499914d7b78$ml$::uuid, $ml$9fd05b5c-e974-5046-9cff-3c16ff1f40ea$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Far more than before$ml$, $ml$NIS2 widened the scope well beyond the first NIS rules, including cloud and data center providers.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$59164d55-65c2-59ee-be7b-62c229f6d32c$ml$::uuid, $ml$9fd05b5c-e974-5046-9cff-3c16ff1f40ea$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Know the reporting clocks$ml$, $ml$Know the clocks: 24 hours for NIS2, four business days for the SEC, 72 hours for GDPR. It makes you useful in an incident.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}, {"url": "https://sec.gov/news/press-release/2023-139", "label": "SEC press release 2023-139"}, {"url": "https://gdpr-text.com/read/article-33/", "label": "GDPR Article 33"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$dd62a12c-0cbc-5775-8502-e9d38e5bf84a$ml$::uuid, $ml$9fd05b5c-e974-5046-9cff-3c16ff1f40ea$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cyber regulation, the reporting clock starts before you know the full story.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}]$ml$::jsonb),
