($ml$62b15a94-7f6c-56f7-b731-b52c4c604e54$ml$::uuid, $ml$c67c2025-c6eb-5ced-939b-6f77d33d3682$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The clock$ml$, $ml$24 hours for an early warning, 48 more for the notification. Then one month for a final report with the root cause.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$5b7ee076-6099-51db-a0dd-9b7cbc446b35$ml$::uuid, $ml$c67c2025-c6eb-5ced-939b-6f77d33d3682$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The stick$ml$, $ml$Fines scale with company size: up to 2% of worldwide turnover. For a big company, that can far exceed €10 million.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$f7fab49a-ff82-55fa-a3a8-9b81dae7a8fc$ml$::uuid, $ml$c67c2025-c6eb-5ced-939b-6f77d33d3682$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Far more than before$ml$, $ml$NIS2 widened the scope well beyond the first NIS rules, including cloud and data center providers.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$f6c756ac-c15b-59b9-b9a6-4d1aca816b57$ml$::uuid, $ml$c67c2025-c6eb-5ced-939b-6f77d33d3682$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Fast reporting needs tools$ml$, $ml$A 24-hour warning leaves little time to gather facts. Tools that speed incident reporting have buyers.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$6d676d60-cf57-5fa1-ba59-bb7190adc2e6$ml$::uuid, $ml$c67c2025-c6eb-5ced-939b-6f77d33d3682$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cyber regulation, the reporting clock starts before you know the full story.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$9eb42f4e-b43b-5ebd-a619-4d921a2ff0d4$ml$::uuid, $ml$17713649-5b73-5cf9-a2af-16d53734ae97$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 17 · The rule$ml$, $ml$Since October 2024, companies under the EU's NIS2 rules must send an early warning within 24 hours of a significant incident. A fuller notification follows within 48 hours of that warning, and a final report within a month. Essential entities face fines of up to €10 million or 2% of worldwide annual turnover, whichever is greater. Important entities face up to €7 million or 1.4%.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$f45dc770-6731-5baa-97ca-123e373582d3$ml$::uuid, $ml$17713649-5b73-5cf9-a2af-16d53734ae97$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The clock$ml$, $ml$24 hours for an early warning, 48 more for the notification. Then one month for a final report with the root cause.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$d982f59c-c123-591b-97ac-0ee7dee257c3$ml$::uuid, $ml$17713649-5b73-5cf9-a2af-16d53734ae97$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The stick$ml$, $ml$Fines scale with company size: up to 2% of worldwide turnover. For a big company, that can far exceed €10 million.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$290ae892-dc43-5624-87d3-947244b680e1$ml$::uuid, $ml$17713649-5b73-5cf9-a2af-16d53734ae97$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Far more than before$ml$, $ml$NIS2 widened the scope well beyond the first NIS rules, including cloud and data center providers.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$75bc3064-8ae2-5997-917b-0861848dcbc8$ml$::uuid, $ml$17713649-5b73-5cf9-a2af-16d53734ae97$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$A day to sound the alarm$ml$, $ml$In the EU, many companies now have just 24 hours to warn authorities about a serious cyber incident.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$44cb0069-2849-5f05-b374-d127d77a97c9$ml$::uuid, $ml$17713649-5b73-5cf9-a2af-16d53734ae97$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cyber regulation, the reporting clock starts before you know the full story.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://wsgr.com/en/insights/nis2-preparing-for-eus-new-cybersecurity-rules.html", "label": "Wilson Sonsini, preparing for the EU's NIS2 rules"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$8d6b19aa-8a80-5173-b1ad-e7bcd3457363$ml$::uuid, $ml$ae42e01a-fab0-54ed-8aae-504e4938d79d$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 18 · Where it breaks$ml$, $ml$In October 2023, the SEC sued SolarWinds and its security chief, Tim Brown, for misleading investors. The SEC said they hid cybersecurity weaknesses from the 2018 IPO until the Russian-linked Sunburst hack came to light in December 2020. In July 2024, a judge dismissed most of the claims. In November 2025, the SEC said it would drop the case. Security leaders had warned it would push people out of CISO jobs.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$3db65852-1769-5b88-9c45-396133c8b2d2$ml$::uuid, $ml$ae42e01a-fab0-54ed-8aae-504e4938d79d$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The charge$ml$, $ml$The claim: public security statements did not match reality. Only claims about the pre-hack Security Statement survived the 2024 ruling.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$5ebf54e0-310e-501f-8a17-5551a0d90a2e$ml$::uuid, $ml$ae42e01a-fab0-54ed-8aae-504e4938d79d$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The pushback$ml$, $ml$Dozens of security leaders opposed the case in 2024. They argued it would hurt security and CISO retention.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$d2b43bcd-d80e-588f-af50-cc3fac0295fc$ml$::uuid, $ml$ae42e01a-fab0-54ed-8aae-504e4938d79d$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$The line is still unclear$ml$, $ml$The case ended without a ruling on how far a security chief is personally responsible for public claims.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$9e224377-4225-5a63-b069-1270e6d4b3b9$ml$::uuid, $ml$ae42e01a-fab0-54ed-8aae-504e4938d79d$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Words in public filings matter$ml$, $ml$The SEC pursued a CISO over security statements. Leaders now check public security claims against reality.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$ffd86a28-d2d1-52ca-9266-df4be03c8488$ml$::uuid, $ml$ae42e01a-fab0-54ed-8aae-504e4938d79d$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cyber, what you say about your security can become a legal risk.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$e6ea722a-666b-56c1-879e-a7a61c9bd693$ml$::uuid, $ml$d696b83b-709c-56e0-813e-f49b71d59d45$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 18 · Where it breaks$ml$, $ml$In October 2023, the SEC sued SolarWinds and its security chief, Tim Brown, for misleading investors. The SEC said they hid cybersecurity weaknesses from the 2018 IPO until the Russian-linked Sunburst hack came to light in December 2020. In July 2024, a judge dismissed most of the claims. In November 2025, the SEC said it would drop the case. Security leaders had warned it would push people out of CISO jobs.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$b811baa1-1373-5f67-bc9b-f9f701b5e320$ml$::uuid, $ml$d696b83b-709c-56e0-813e-f49b71d59d45$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The charge$ml$, $ml$The claim: public security statements did not match reality. Only claims about the pre-hack Security Statement survived the 2024 ruling.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$5d520c11-9ad9-516a-b570-1ae3532eda86$ml$::uuid, $ml$d696b83b-709c-56e0-813e-f49b71d59d45$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The pushback$ml$, $ml$Dozens of security leaders opposed the case in 2024. They argued it would hurt security and CISO retention.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$f7156cab-9373-5354-894b-eb31c7cfa6d0$ml$::uuid, $ml$d696b83b-709c-56e0-813e-f49b71d59d45$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$The line is still unclear$ml$, $ml$The case ended without a ruling on how far a security chief is personally responsible for public claims.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$44545a0c-07b5-5a5c-9f3e-cedd9b197faa$ml$::uuid, $ml$d696b83b-709c-56e0-813e-f49b71d59d45$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Disclosure risk is real$ml$, $ml$Security claims in filings can bring regulators. Watch how companies describe their security to investors.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$ea7c1ec5-9e1c-5d0a-8a6e-9737643ab85d$ml$::uuid, $ml$d696b83b-709c-56e0-813e-f49b71d59d45$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cyber, what you say about your security can become a legal risk.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$94bd06c8-a724-5c80-aa59-76849147d3c7$ml$::uuid, $ml$02cea5b6-2859-5263-a22b-1a6c97ad978d$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 18 · Where it breaks$ml$, $ml$In October 2023, the SEC sued SolarWinds and its security chief, Tim Brown, for misleading investors. The SEC said they hid cybersecurity weaknesses from the 2018 IPO until the Russian-linked Sunburst hack came to light in December 2020. In July 2024, a judge dismissed most of the claims. In November 2025, the SEC said it would drop the case. Security leaders had warned it would push people out of CISO jobs.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$3d5997fc-ba2e-5200-ae5d-cfe7f3a63edb$ml$::uuid, $ml$02cea5b6-2859-5263-a22b-1a6c97ad978d$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The charge$ml$, $ml$The claim: public security statements did not match reality. Only claims about the pre-hack Security Statement survived the 2024 ruling.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$113cc2b8-faa9-5b0d-9557-a5c732d67119$ml$::uuid, $ml$02cea5b6-2859-5263-a22b-1a6c97ad978d$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The pushback$ml$, $ml$Dozens of security leaders opposed the case in 2024. They argued it would hurt security and CISO retention.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$66bdd017-eece-5a32-af0b-bc98592dae95$ml$::uuid, $ml$02cea5b6-2859-5263-a22b-1a6c97ad978d$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$The line is still unclear$ml$, $ml$The case ended without a ruling on how far a security chief is personally responsible for public claims.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$1a8b918a-dcf2-564b-addc-4cbccb418b8d$ml$::uuid, $ml$02cea5b6-2859-5263-a22b-1a6c97ad978d$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Say only what is true$ml$, $ml$Marketing about your security can become evidence. Keep public claims as precise as your controls.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$1452a391-7ffd-5507-92d8-ad1ea42b9767$ml$::uuid, $ml$02cea5b6-2859-5263-a22b-1a6c97ad978d$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cyber, what you say about your security can become a legal risk.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$8c9b30aa-88e7-5e48-a6bd-309da675d942$ml$::uuid, $ml$5a05437e-c764-5927-bd53-26d977af36fc$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 18 · Where it breaks$ml$, $ml$In October 2023, the SEC sued SolarWinds and its security chief, Tim Brown, for misleading investors. The SEC said they hid cybersecurity weaknesses from the 2018 IPO until the Russian-linked Sunburst hack came to light in December 2020. In July 2024, a judge dismissed most of the claims. In November 2025, the SEC said it would drop the case. Security leaders had warned it would push people out of CISO jobs.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$866ac2b4-7ad3-5412-b5f1-27c79a663af2$ml$::uuid, $ml$5a05437e-c764-5927-bd53-26d977af36fc$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The charge$ml$, $ml$The claim: public security statements did not match reality. Only claims about the pre-hack Security Statement survived the 2024 ruling.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$835ed414-3a7e-54d3-8fae-40ddf58ef5b6$ml$::uuid, $ml$5a05437e-c764-5927-bd53-26d977af36fc$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The pushback$ml$, $ml$Dozens of security leaders opposed the case in 2024. They argued it would hurt security and CISO retention.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$87d78274-ab7e-5108-8ef3-b04d944b45c8$ml$::uuid, $ml$5a05437e-c764-5927-bd53-26d977af36fc$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$The line is still unclear$ml$, $ml$The case ended without a ruling on how far a security chief is personally responsible for public claims.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$0460a01f-c711-5fd3-b105-4da9c1771c14$ml$::uuid, $ml$5a05437e-c764-5927-bd53-26d977af36fc$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$A CISO in court$ml$, $ml$For two years, a security chief faced an SEC lawsuit over what his company said about its security.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$77f9d977-36db-5284-9782-43bad3aa125d$ml$::uuid, $ml$5a05437e-c764-5927-bd53-26d977af36fc$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cyber, what you say about your security can become a legal risk.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.nextgov.com/cybersecurity/2025/11/sec-drop-high-profile-solarwinds-hack-lawsuit/409684/", "label": "Nextgov, SEC to drop SolarWinds lawsuit"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$022d646b-5f1b-502e-9b05-aef984d6060d$ml$::uuid, $ml$37efa5bd-9d12-582c-8948-0d91a93081cd$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 19 · Identity$ml$, $ml$Credential abuse was the top way into breaches in Verizon's 2025 report, at 22%. Exploited software flaws were close behind at 20%. Identity and access management decides two things: authentication, proving who you are, and authorization, deciding what you may do once you are in. When attackers steal a login, both checks can wave them through.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$4955f201-119f-58a9-9cf7-9d4b465a9eca$ml$::uuid, $ml$37efa5bd-9d12-582c-8948-0d91a93081cd$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$Step 1$ml$, $ml$Authentication proves who you are: a password, a code, a fingerprint. Multifactor authentication asks for two or more of these.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$480cd4f4-d741-541b-8336-ab6f18ce1378$ml$::uuid, $ml$37efa5bd-9d12-582c-8948-0d91a93081cd$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$Step 2$ml$, $ml$Authorization decides what you can reach once you are in. Giving each account only what it needs limits the damage.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$79ae7304-45b0-5007-a90b-9eca1730be5a$ml$::uuid, $ml$37efa5bd-9d12-582c-8948-0d91a93081cd$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Stolen logins look legitimate$ml$, $ml$An attacker with real credentials can look like a normal user. That is why identity is now a core security layer.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$132f86ba-d5b5-5efe-b36c-282228e96994$ml$::uuid, $ml$37efa5bd-9d12-582c-8948-0d91a93081cd$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Separate the two checks$ml$, $ml$Explain authentication versus authorization clearly. It is a staple interview question in security.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$643b75d8-af05-59dc-aebc-75a359f786e0$ml$::uuid, $ml$37efa5bd-9d12-582c-8948-0d91a93081cd$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cyber, identity is the new perimeter: protect the login and you protect the door.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$0fb9d4ad-ed73-5b9a-a328-8f78177eb6a2$ml$::uuid, $ml$d4a4af06-6a48-5bc5-a1cd-1fcec2fc449c$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 19 · Identity$ml$, $ml$Credential abuse was the top way into breaches in Verizon's 2025 report, at 22%. Exploited software flaws were close behind at 20%. Identity and access management decides two things: authentication, proving who you are, and authorization, deciding what you may do once you are in. When attackers steal a login, both checks can wave them through.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$c28c28a5-a8af-5ec1-836e-357a83c4b7f3$ml$::uuid, $ml$d4a4af06-6a48-5bc5-a1cd-1fcec2fc449c$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$Step 1$ml$, $ml$Authentication proves who you are: a password, a code, a fingerprint. Multifactor authentication asks for two or more of these.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
