($ml$6b182a29-25ba-544a-a77b-c50582c9d295$ml$::uuid, $ml$d4a4af06-6a48-5bc5-a1cd-1fcec2fc449c$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Identity is the front line$ml$, $ml$Credential abuse led breaches in 2025. Spending follows to identity tools.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$bec1bf42-080c-57e8-9471-eb41b39300a2$ml$::uuid, $ml$d4a4af06-6a48-5bc5-a1cd-1fcec2fc449c$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cyber, identity is the new perimeter: protect the login and you protect the door.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$8a1c1cd8-097e-55b3-a4b8-9f3d3c066eb0$ml$::uuid, $ml$1d522c35-0692-569a-b7e8-26a9d0fb0999$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 19 · Identity$ml$, $ml$Credential abuse was the top way into breaches in Verizon's 2025 report, at 22%. Exploited software flaws were close behind at 20%. Identity and access management decides two things: authentication, proving who you are, and authorization, deciding what you may do once you are in. When attackers steal a login, both checks can wave them through.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$11c86ae7-f4d6-5ab5-86a5-31dadf94cc1f$ml$::uuid, $ml$1d522c35-0692-569a-b7e8-26a9d0fb0999$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$Step 1$ml$, $ml$Authentication proves who you are: a password, a code, a fingerprint. Multifactor authentication asks for two or more of these.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$d6d8326b-5ef5-50cd-9419-c7ae21ba5a15$ml$::uuid, $ml$1d522c35-0692-569a-b7e8-26a9d0fb0999$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$Step 2$ml$, $ml$Authorization decides what you can reach once you are in. Giving each account only what it needs limits the damage.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$8f7447f1-9ba3-5aa2-85b5-e041e1cf770c$ml$::uuid, $ml$1d522c35-0692-569a-b7e8-26a9d0fb0999$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Stolen logins look legitimate$ml$, $ml$An attacker with real credentials can look like a normal user. That is why identity is now a core security layer.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$55bf5d20-4436-511d-af23-e71673bc162f$ml$::uuid, $ml$1d522c35-0692-569a-b7e8-26a9d0fb0999$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Stolen logins are the pain$ml$, $ml$When attackers log in with real credentials, spotting them is hard. That gap keeps identity startups busy.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$8d5a3e29-ae68-5cf7-96e0-5afaaa606638$ml$::uuid, $ml$1d522c35-0692-569a-b7e8-26a9d0fb0999$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cyber, identity is the new perimeter: protect the login and you protect the door.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$fdc3416f-67b6-5db8-a6a3-e7b59c731250$ml$::uuid, $ml$f0f61e7c-0ce8-5316-8c15-5d427882abd4$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 19 · Identity$ml$, $ml$Credential abuse was the top way into breaches in Verizon's 2025 report, at 22%. Exploited software flaws were close behind at 20%. Identity and access management decides two things: authentication, proving who you are, and authorization, deciding what you may do once you are in. When attackers steal a login, both checks can wave them through.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$214313f0-6156-5bbb-85d3-c35ecdb05892$ml$::uuid, $ml$f0f61e7c-0ce8-5316-8c15-5d427882abd4$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$Step 1$ml$, $ml$Authentication proves who you are: a password, a code, a fingerprint. Multifactor authentication asks for two or more of these.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
