($ml$81e990df-37dd-5e0a-9e45-4018468701ba$ml$::uuid, $ml$f0f61e7c-0ce8-5316-8c15-5d427882abd4$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Stolen logins look legitimate$ml$, $ml$An attacker with real credentials can look like a normal user. That is why identity is now a core security layer.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$4f985929-4c00-5396-a5b6-d62a97740435$ml$::uuid, $ml$f0f61e7c-0ce8-5316-8c15-5d427882abd4$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Logging in, not breaking in$ml$, $ml$More breaches in 2025 started with a stolen login than with any other method.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$88ef6139-337d-5247-b0f4-a6176a3b1a11$ml$::uuid, $ml$f0f61e7c-0ce8-5316-8c15-5d427882abd4$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cyber, identity is the new perimeter: protect the login and you protect the door.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025%2Ddata%2Dbreach%2Dinvestigations%2Dreport", "label": "Verizon, 2025 Data Breach Investigations Report"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$c6fd9ef0-741c-5e19-a69e-8e23793ddeaa$ml$::uuid, $ml$56a35fce-c1f0-5f4b-aaf1-5dc3e1ddffeb$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 20 · The money$ml$, $ml$In July 2025, Palo Alto Networks agreed to buy CyberArk, an identity security company, for about $25 billion. CyberArk protects privileged accounts, the logins with the most power inside a company. Palo Alto offered $45 in cash plus 2.2005 of its own shares for each CyberArk share, a 26% premium. Its CEO pointed to AI and an explosion of machine identities as reasons for the deal.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.intelligentcio.com/north-america/2025/07/30/palo-alto-networks-to-acquire-cyberark-in-25-billion-deal-to-expand-identity-security-and-ai-protection/", "label": "Intelligent CIO, Palo Alto Networks to acquire CyberArk"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$276e0875-fb20-56c8-987b-a34945221cf5$ml$::uuid, $ml$56a35fce-c1f0-5f4b-aaf1-5dc3e1ddffeb$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$What it protects$ml$, $ml$Privileged accounts can change systems, read everything or turn defenses off. They are what attackers want most once inside.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.intelligentcio.com/north-america/2025/07/30/palo-alto-networks-to-acquire-cyberark-in-25-billion-deal-to-expand-identity-security-and-ai-protection/", "label": "Intelligent CIO, Palo Alto Networks to acquire CyberArk"}]$ml$::jsonb),
