($ml$b1935c46-bfbb-5672-9a72-910429a61987$ml$::uuid, $ml$da514d19-1c54-5f19-aee8-3ee3fad2d70b$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The weak point$ml$, $ml$Whoever can reset a password holds power over every account. Help desks exist to say yes to stressed callers.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.adaptivesecurity.com/blog/mgm-ransomware-attack", "label": "Adaptive Security, the MGM attack, citing MGM filings"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$dcadba6e-af0a-5461-a4c8-d1deffd75ef9$ml$::uuid, $ml$da514d19-1c54-5f19-aee8-3ee3fad2d70b$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The claim$ml$, $ml$The attackers said the call took about 10 minutes. That account has not been confirmed by investigators.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.adaptivesecurity.com/blog/mgm-ransomware-attack", "label": "Adaptive Security, the MGM attack, citing MGM filings"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$4edfbec8-2343-5162-a2aa-50854d85a817$ml$::uuid, $ml$da514d19-1c54-5f19-aee8-3ee3fad2d70b$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$English-speaking social engineers$ml$, $ml$Microsoft describes Scattered Spider as financially motivated and native English-speaking, which makes their calls convincing.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.adaptivesecurity.com/blog/mgm-ransomware-attack", "label": "Adaptive Security, the MGM attack, citing MGM filings"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$cd5aef86-fd01-5914-9dcb-58c7a8d872af$ml$::uuid, $ml$da514d19-1c54-5f19-aee8-3ee3fad2d70b$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$A call that cost millions$ml$, $ml$Attackers claimed a 10-minute call to a help desk opened the door to a $100 million hit.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.adaptivesecurity.com/blog/mgm-ransomware-attack", "label": "Adaptive Security, the MGM attack, citing MGM filings"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$aad51252-51db-57d0-808e-2ddeb37e3605$ml$::uuid, $ml$da514d19-1c54-5f19-aee8-3ee3fad2d70b$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cyber, whoever can reset access holds the real power.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.adaptivesecurity.com/blog/mgm-ransomware-attack", "label": "Adaptive Security, the MGM attack, citing MGM filings"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$c77f4c91-daca-53e9-b156-ca44da8eaf29$ml$::uuid, $ml$df6d4c22-f591-5ffc-8944-c80cc90a3a1b$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 22 · The numbers$ml$, $ml$Microsoft researchers found MFA reduces the risk of account compromise by 99.22%. They studied a large set of Microsoft Azure Active Directory users who showed suspicious activity. Even for accounts whose passwords had already leaked, MFA cut the risk of compromise by 98.56%. Few security controls move a number that far.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.00945", "label": "Microsoft researchers, how effective is MFA"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$6a7df3dc-3c7e-5f35-9eaa-9067615c7790$ml$::uuid, $ml$df6d4c22-f591-5ffc-8944-c80cc90a3a1b$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$Even after a leak$ml$, $ml$A leaked password alone was usually not enough with MFA on. Risk fell by 98.56% for those accounts.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.00945", "label": "Microsoft researchers, how effective is MFA"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$7f12ba95-68ee-56bf-b937-9b8feec12497$ml$::uuid, $ml$df6d4c22-f591-5ffc-8944-c80cc90a3a1b$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The trade$ml$, $ml$MFA adds a few seconds per login. In exchange it removes almost all account takeover risk.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.00945", "label": "Microsoft researchers, how effective is MFA"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$83b974b4-2a8d-516b-9810-c009705791b4$ml$::uuid, $ml$df6d4c22-f591-5ffc-8944-c80cc90a3a1b$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Not all MFA is equal$ml$, $ml$Codes and push prompts can still be phished or approved by mistake. Stronger forms resist that.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.00945", "label": "Microsoft researchers, how effective is MFA"}, {"url": "https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/M-22-09.pdf", "label": "OMB memo M-22-09, federal zero trust strategy"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$f78963d6-2722-5c88-b0a4-18b6cb89d726$ml$::uuid, $ml$df6d4c22-f591-5ffc-8944-c80cc90a3a1b$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Quote the MFA number$ml$, $ml$99.22% fewer compromises with MFA. It is the strongest single argument in account security.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.00945", "label": "Microsoft researchers, how effective is MFA"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$5c379f56-af75-5dbb-8f51-548fa4acaa59$ml$::uuid, $ml$df6d4c22-f591-5ffc-8944-c80cc90a3a1b$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cyber, the cheapest controls are often the ones that matter most.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.00945", "label": "Microsoft researchers, how effective is MFA"}]$ml$::jsonb),
