($ml$65e36220-59f3-586b-8a23-8ca503d6573e$ml$::uuid, $ml$34e48d3b-815d-5ef2-b616-b5e0373fbfa9$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 30 · Where it breaks$ml$, $ml$In August 2024, NIST published its first three post-quantum encryption standards. FIPS 203 covers general encryption, and FIPS 204 and FIPS 205 cover digital signatures. They are built to resist future quantum computers that could break much of today's encryption. The worry is harvest now, decrypt later: attackers collect encrypted data today and read it once such machines exist.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.hklaw.com/en/insights/publications/2024/08/nist-releases-three-post-quantum-cryptography-standards", "label": "Holland & Knight, NIST post-quantum standards"}]$ml$::jsonb),
