($ml$9b6ba19b-8220-5e08-991e-244e2578070a$ml$::uuid, $ml$617c38fb-7c7b-5133-af76-11fdda570b4d$ml$::uuid, 1, $ml$Day 30 · Where it breaks$ml$, $ml$In August 2024, NIST published its first three post-quantum encryption standards. FIPS 203 covers general encryption, and FIPS 204 and FIPS 205 cover digital signatures. They are built to resist future quantum computers that could break much of today's encryption. The worry is harvest now, decrypt later: attackers collect encrypted data today and read it once such machines exist.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.hklaw.com/en/insights/publications/2024/08/nist-releases-three-post-quantum-cryptography-standards", "label": "Holland & Knight, NIST post-quantum standards"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$7eae9cc9-5d3b-5436-b875-c5ec0f0e595f$ml$::uuid, $ml$617c38fb-7c7b-5133-af76-11fdda570b4d$ml$::uuid, 2, $ml$The threat$ml$, $ml$Data stolen today can be decrypted years from now. Secrets that must last a decade are already at risk.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.hklaw.com/en/insights/publications/2024/08/nist-releases-three-post-quantum-cryptography-standards", "label": "Holland & Knight, NIST post-quantum standards"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$77254dbc-68f1-5f60-9faf-e81f58a5a332$ml$::uuid, $ml$617c38fb-7c7b-5133-af76-11fdda570b4d$ml$::uuid, 3, $ml$The clock$ml$, $ml$The release started a one-year clock for further federal guidance. Agencies are expected to migrate quickly once that guidance lands.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.hklaw.com/en/insights/publications/2024/08/nist-releases-three-post-quantum-cryptography-standards", "label": "Holland & Knight, NIST post-quantum standards"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$f052e652-ed63-59b9-be47-219ca3111cff$ml$::uuid, $ml$617c38fb-7c7b-5133-af76-11fdda570b4d$ml$::uuid, 4, $ml$Finding all the old encryption$ml$, $ml$Companies must first find every place they use vulnerable encryption before they can replace it.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.hklaw.com/en/insights/publications/2024/08/nist-releases-three-post-quantum-cryptography-standards", "label": "Holland & Knight, NIST post-quantum standards"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$7cc6723f-270c-5395-9dc9-e8c4cf8cb875$ml$::uuid, $ml$617c38fb-7c7b-5133-af76-11fdda570b4d$ml$::uuid, 5, $ml$Codes for future computers$ml$, $ml$Encryption is being rebuilt now to resist computers that do not fully exist yet.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.hklaw.com/en/insights/publications/2024/08/nist-releases-three-post-quantum-cryptography-standards", "label": "Holland & Knight, NIST post-quantum standards"}]$ml$::jsonb),
($ml$7fbb4586-2ed3-587c-8d76-38215cf8dd1b$ml$::uuid, $ml$617c38fb-7c7b-5133-af76-11fdda570b4d$ml$::uuid, 6, $ml$The rule$ml$, $ml$In cryptography, you protect today's secrets against tomorrow's machines.$ml$, $ml$[{"url": "https://www.hklaw.com/en/insights/publications/2024/08/nist-releases-three-post-quantum-cryptography-standards", "label": "Holland & Knight, NIST post-quantum standards"}]$ml$::jsonb);
